; Deliberately unhealthy A/B trial candidate. IN-HOUSE INSTRUMENT, NEVER SHIPPED.
;
; The loader arms a 15-second trial watchdog at L0 and hands it to the payload
; at L6. A healthy candidate confirms its generation and stops that watchdog;
; this one enters, says exactly what it is, and then parks forever without
; confirming anything. The hardware watchdog must therefore reset the board, and
; the loader must see a TRIED record with no CONFIRMED and boot the previously
; confirmed slot instead.
;
; It deliberately does NOT call Pi3UpdateBootStart: it must not mount storage,
; touch a control record or write anything at all. Everything it needs - the
; PL011 already configured by the loader - it was handed.
;
; Same placement as the real updater slot, because the loader copies a slot to
; its recorded entry address and the P3SLOT wrapper checks it exactly.
LoadAddress $200000
BssAddress $1100000
StackAddress $1F00000
#ANVIL_BUILD = 0 ; pmf:build off
#ANVIL_BUILD_DATE = 20260918 ; pmf:builddate
#ANVIL_BUILD_TIME = 172500 ; pmf:buildtime
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi3/Board/update_boot_support.pbi"
Procedure Main()
  pi3_dtb = $1000000
  pi3ut_WriteLine("C0: candidate Main entered")
  pi3ut_WriteLine("WDT: unhealthy trial candidate; it will never confirm, so the 15-second trial watchdog must reset this board")
  pi3ut_WriteLine("WDT: parking now; the next thing on this port should be the loader, booting the confirmed slot")
  Pi3Park()
EndProcedure
